amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-17T06:25:33-07:00","id":1495116,"title":"","content":"I said this in the Reddit thread but, I'll also post it here.<br /> <br /> In the Skinner Reborn module, it talks about the pelts the Skin Dancers have and how they no longer need to hunt werewolves because they have killed all these Ronin and BSD so they have enough pelts that a Kinfolk just coming in can become a full Gerou.<br /> <br /> The Wyrm Taint from the pelts (since they were not given willingly) are just going to stay there regardless of how much Cleansing you do though arguably with merit/flaws 'Wyrm-Touched' and 'Wyrm Tainted' makes me wonder how many normal Fera just are wyrmy just by existing.<br /> <br /> That said, if you were going to do this 'your sins are already forgiven' kind of Catholic Crusade against evil, I think it could be an interesting story. I think it really doesn't matter if its mechanically fine, socially and culturally the Gaian Garou wouldn't be cool with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-17T09:26:37-07:00","id":1495122,"title":"","content":"The nature of Wyrm taint and Rite of Cleansing is something that can be heavily dependent on ST interpretation. It is not the case that Rite of Cleansing permanently cleanses an area. It can provided the extent of Wyrm Taint is rather low and its source has been completely removed. However, if the Wyrm taint is at a higher level or the reason for its existence is ongoing, the Rite of Cleansing might only be the equivalent of dropping some bleach into a mass of sewage - it's not going to cleanse/purge anything really.<br /> <br /> I think that can be obviously seen in a situation where a drainage pipe is dumping huge volumes of some tainted pollution. Most players would agree that performing a Rite of Cleansing is insufficient. To be effective first you have to stop the source of pollution so that nothing more is flowing in, and second, you likely have to remove the pollution that is already in the area. You pretty much have to wait until the Superfund clean up occurs before a Rite of Cleansing can eliminate the Wyrm taint entirely. Doing it beforehand while the pollution is still present might temporarily make the area unattractive to Banes, but very soon the Wyrm taint will creep back in.<br /> <br /> But what about the issue of the Garou skins themselves? Do they just need one Rite of Cleansing and they are free of all taint forever? Does each skin have various amounts of Wyrm traint depending on the nature of its &quot;harvesting&quot;, meaning certain skins require more before they are cleansed entirely? Or are all skins permanently and forever tainted because its a perversion of Gaia's natural order?<br /> <br /> Different STs and different gaming groups will come to different conclusions. I know some players (perhaps the OP as well) think it's the first scenario. In my chronicles, it's the third scenario. And as such, the Skindancers could never be accepted by any of the Gaian totems of the Garou Nation. Stag, Pegasus, Bear, Boar, etc. simply will never adopt them as children of their own, whether as packs or tribes regardless of their intentions or motives. The Skindancers are stuck with dubious totems like Minotaur and some other candidates, and they will always be on the outside of the Garou Nation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-17T10:00:20-07:00","id":1495125,"title":"","content":"I also think it would be the third scenario but, I don't know if I would agree with the totems themselves not accepting any Skin-Dancers. According to the Outcast book they have two Caerns one whose totem are &quot;Trickster&quot; the other &quot;Magpie.&quot; It's really questionable the relationship is between the Skin-Dancers and the totems (since it really only briefly talks about them) but, I have to assume that the totem accepts them. What this actually means to the nature of Skin-Dancers and spirits I'm not actually sure but, it seems to me that Skin-Dancers are not outright rejected by Gaian Spirits and have the ability to treat with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-17T13:32:50-07:00","id":1495138,"title":"","content":"Ronin are still Garou, and there are many spirits that would be willing to have followers and offer patronage to agents in the living world. However, I still don't see the stain of Skin Dancing ever washing off. Being a Ronin is being a social outcast that is punished by the Garou by ostracism. Being a Skin Dancer is being insane enough to do a wyrmish rite that kills other Garou to make you into a fascimile of a Garou. In my eyes the Skin Walkers may mechanically work like Garou, but they're not much further from a Mockery Breed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-17T13:46:00-07:00","id":1495139,"title":"","content":"While there's some variations in results depending on where you pick things in the metaplot/etc. The Skin-Dancers are canonically capable of getting a Tribal Totem if they work for it. Both of the options, Minotaur and Tick, are like the Skin Dancers themselves, caught in a bad place as both are closely aligned with many spirits that fell to the Wyrm, but aren't (or at least until certain characters change things) fully fallen to the Wyrm either. It still makes the default assumption (at least for now) that the Skin Dancers are capable of becoming a full Tribe with the necessary spiritual bonds to a Totem; even if whether they've successfully managed to do so yet has come to pass in your games or not. <br /> <br /> Once they do form a Tribe (if that's where the table takes things) then individuals renouncing the Tribe, or being kicked out of it, are options to consider.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-21T11:11:07-07:00","id":1495362,"title":"","content":"It's an honest shame that Kinfolk who are competent enough to murder five Garou under exceptionally stringent conditions, which is an insane combination if a horribly hard to kill target and a very difficult pattern of serial killing to maintain, and also achieve Rituals 5 and master a level 5 Rite when Kinfolk are ostracized from such knowledge almost entirely, are left with so little to make of their talents by the Garou Nation that becoming a Skin Dancer is even vaguely appealing.<br /> <br /> Seriously, becoming a Skin Dancer (without help) might just be one of the hardest things to pull off in the WoD. Whoever achieves it with even a vaguely competent Sept around them is a once in a generation genius who, in a sane and equitable society, would be sat at the top table helping with grand matters of strategy, counter-espionage and so on.<br /> <br /> So to me the interesting thing about Skin Dancers isn't the Dancers themselves. A story about them becoming a Tribe or being purified feels like it misses the point. The root problem is that someone with such an insane generational talent was left to whither on the vine until they stole a leading role in their own story by ending five others. It shows how deep corruption and wasted potential run within the Garou nation, how little care is taken of Kinfolk, how little their true potential is leveraged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-21T13:54:17-07:00","id":1495370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494970-rite-of-renunciation-and-skin-dancers?p=1495362#post1495362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's an honest shame that Kinfolk who are competent enough to murder five Garou under exceptionally stringent conditions, which is an insane combination if a horribly hard to kill target and a very difficult pattern of serial killing to maintain, and also achieve Rituals 5 and master a level 5 Rite when Kinfolk are ostracized from such knowledge almost entirely, are left with so little to make of their talents by the Garou Nation that becoming a Skin Dancer is even vaguely appealing.<br /> <br /> Seriously, becoming a Skin Dancer (without help) might just be one of the hardest things to pull off in the WoD. Whoever achieves it with even a vaguely competent Sept around them is a once in a generation genius who, in a sane and equitable society, would be sat at the top table helping with grand matters of strategy, counter-espionage and so on.<br /> <br /> So to me the interesting thing about Skin Dancers isn't the Dancers themselves. A story about them becoming a Tribe or being purified feels like it misses the point. The root problem is that someone with such an insane generational talent was left to whither on the vine until they stole a leading role in their own story by ending five others. It shows how deep corruption and wasted potential run within the Garou nation, how little care is taken of Kinfolk, how little their true potential is leveraged.</div> </div> </div> </div>*concerned face*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-21T14:54:19-07:00","id":1495373,"title":"","content":"Honestly... murdering Garou isn't that hard if you know what you're doing; esp. for kin that have easier access to the Garou and are more likely to know the requisite things to understand how to isolate and murder a Garou before they can Rage out and kill you.<br /> <br /> Both Unsung Heroes and even more so A Breed Apart made it so Rituals was more commonly known to kinfolk. Yes Rituals 5 is still a lot, but one of the reasons that the Skin Dancers can be a thing instead of just one guy doing it, is that the Garou are supposed to be dying off, and that puts more pressure on the kinfolk to maintain knowledge; kin can learn Rituals and even individual rites they can't actually use (or use and expect any results), letting them pass on such knowledge in places where there aren't enough Garou to consistently have Garou mentors for everything.<br /> <br /> The restrictions on the killing pattern also aren't that hard: all five have to be the same Auspice. Killing five cubs that are between their First Change and their initiatons, or killing five Elders of the same moon phase doesn't actually change anything.<br /> <br /> This is not to say that the process is easy, but it can be done by people that aren't such incredibly badass geniuses that you'd consider overlooking their actions for how good they should be made leaders because it's that impressive doesn't really hold up.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-21T15:39:51-07:00","id":1495380,"title":"","content":"I still have issues perceiving them as a tribe. There cannot be more than a dozen of them in the world. How do they even qualify?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-21T15:55:09-07:00","id":1495381,"title":"","content":"There can't really by that many Siberakh either, but they're effectively a Tribe. According to one of the books there's only ~200 Stargazers.<br /> <br /> The problem is that WtA wasn't designed to have something like Bloodlines to provide a space for off-shoots of the Tribes that mechanically take Tribe's place on character sheet, but imply a different narrative position.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-21T17:56:41-07:00","id":1495394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494970-rite-of-renunciation-and-skin-dancers?p=1495381#post1495381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There can't really by that many Siberakh either, but they're effectively a Tribe. According to one of the books there's only ~200 Stargazers.<br /> <br /> The problem is that WtA wasn't designed to have something like Bloodlines to provide a space for off-shoots of the Tribes that mechanically take Tribe's place on character sheet, but imply a different narrative position.</div> </div> </div> </div>A subset of Camps do fulfill a similar function and you have groups like the Singing Dogs and Kucha Ekundu but the coverage was fairly spotty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T23:57:48-07:00","id":1495468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494970-rite-of-renunciation-and-skin-dancers?p=1495373#post1495373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly... murdering Garou isn't that hard if you know what you're doing; esp. for kin that have easier access to the Garou and are more likely to know the requisite things to understand how to isolate and murder a Garou before they can Rage out and kill you.<br /> <br /> Both Unsung Heroes and even more so A Breed Apart made it so Rituals was more commonly known to kinfolk. Yes Rituals 5 is still a lot, but one of the reasons that the Skin Dancers can be a thing instead of just one guy doing it, is that the Garou are supposed to be dying off, and that puts more pressure on the kinfolk to maintain knowledge; kin can learn Rituals and even individual rites they can't actually use (or use and expect any results), letting them pass on such knowledge in places where there aren't enough Garou to consistently have Garou mentors for everything.<br /> <br /> The restrictions on the killing pattern also aren't that hard: all five have to be the same Auspice. Killing five cubs that are between their First Change and their initiatons, or killing five Elders of the same moon phase doesn't actually change anything.<br /> <br /> This is not to say that the process is easy, but it can be done by people that aren't such incredibly badass geniuses that you'd consider overlooking their actions for how good they should be made leaders because it's that impressive doesn't really hold up.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point isn't that you should forgive them of their crimes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Seriously, becoming a Skin Dancer (without help) might just be one of the hardest things to pull off in the WoD. Whoever achieves it with even a vaguely competent Sept around them is a once in a generation genius who, in a sane and equitable society, would be sat at the top table helping with grand matters of strategy, counter-espionage and so on.<br /> <br /> So to me the interesting thing about Skin Dancers isn't the Dancers themselves. A story about them becoming a Tribe or being purified feels like it misses the point. The root problem is that someone with such an insane generational talent was left to whither on the vine until they stole a leading role in their own story by ending five others. It shows how deep corruption and wasted potential run within the Garou nation, how little care is taken of Kinfolk, how little their true potential is leveraged. </div> </div> </div>The point is that these are people who could have, in a society that treats Kinfolk as equal (if different), been of great use to the nation. The existence of Skin Dancers is a symptom of Kinfolk being made to feel inferior, and a symptom of the most competent and talented Kinfolk being left with their abilities under-utilized. Skin Dancers didn't just pop into existence, they are a reflection of problems within the Tribes.<br /> <br /> Also the rite is a little harder than you think it is - you need to gather each hide under the same moon phase. So if you do your first murder under the gibbous moon, then all the other murders have to be performed under that moon too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Each of the hides must be taken under the same lunar phase; if the first werewolf slain by the Skin Dancer was slain under a gibbous moon, all subsequent hides must be gathered under a gibbous moon for the rite to be enacted successfully. The final ceremony of the rite must be conducted under a moon that matches the phase under which the hides were claimed and preserved, and must conclude exactly an hour after it is initiated. </div> </div> </div>Like I said before, pulling this off with even a vaguely competent Sept around you for even 2 of the murders would be insanely difficult. Garou have detective powers that make this sort of thing very difficult. Easy mode, attacking cubs? Even if you go after the least cared-for cubs, or Ronin, the loss of such young Garou with all their potential untapped would still create an uproar. And Garou are horribly strong at all power levels; their base kit, being able to go Crinos/Hispo, makes them a huge threat even with no Gifts, even with mediocre Rage.<br /> <br /> Plus if you are able to pick the easiest targets and hunt them down efficiently with minimal risk that only furthers the point I'm making; you met your objective with the smartest strategy available and you've shown skill in backing up your idea, hunting down the best possible candidates for an easy execution. Again, skills the Garou Nation could have benefited from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 10-23-2022, 03:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-23T00:06:08-07:00","id":1495469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494970-rite-of-renunciation-and-skin-dancers?p=1495394#post1495394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A subset of Camps do fulfill a similar function and you have groups like the Singing Dogs and Kucha Ekundu but the coverage was fairly spotty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah was gonna mention the Singing Dogs - they do technically meet the definition of a Tribe, but they are a &quot;Tribe&quot; made up of one Pack. It feels like it depends on your definition at that point, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-23T00:12:45-07:00","id":1495470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494970-rite-of-renunciation-and-skin-dancers?p=1495370#post1495370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *concerned face*</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One of the most often overlooked threats to the Garou Nation is the ever-increasing number of Kinfolk who, driven by feelings of inferiority and resentment towards their Garou relations, turn on their families. These Kin are motivated by vicious desperation, hungry for a birthright they feel has been denied them: the First Change. For centuries, Garou turned a blind eye to the discontent of these Kin; there was nothing the Kinfolk could do but complain about the unfairness of it all. There\u2019s no way for a Kin to become Garou, they knew. Gaia alone can create a new shapechanger. They were wrong. </div> </div> </div>As per W20 the Garou know that Kinfolk can be jealous, resentful, wishing they could do more, and the Garou have (and continue to do so arguably) turned a blind eye. The writeup in W20 shows that the toxic cocktail of resentment, Wyrmish whispers, fratricide and so on doesn't come out of nowhere, and the beginning of the section immediately talks about Garou failing to address the growing discontent.<br /> <br /> It isn't that Skin Dancers are misunderstood geniuses who just needed more hugs. It's that the mere existence of such Kinfolk who would seek to follow that path is a sign that the Garou Nation has gotten their approach to Kinfolk wrong. Hell, the whole Kinfolk book in W20 is harping on that fact repeatedly!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-23T02:15:21-07:00","id":1495472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494970-rite-of-renunciation-and-skin-dancers?p=1495468#post1495468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point isn't that you should forgive them of their crimes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said it was.<br /> <br /> More importantly, your hyperbolic statements aren't really going anywhere productive. You're the one that's painting Skindancers as such bad asses that they should be in charge, not me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The point is that these are people who could have, in a society that treats Kinfolk as equal (if different), been of great use to the nation. </div> </div> </div>Um... yeah? That's sort of the whole point? The Garou have taken their kin for granted for generations, and it's finally biting them in the ass even as Garou that saw this coming and have worked to avoid it are doing their own thing too. Between Camps and Kin Fellowships, there are multiple ways kin can gain higher standing in the nation and contribute these skills in a productive fashion instead of murdering the people they want to impressive. It's not like the characters in the setting are blind to why the Skin Dancers became a thing. It's just an awareness that's too little and too late, and the genie is out of the bottle.<br /> <br /> Nobody's' contesting the idea that Skin Dancers are a symptom of the systemic and institutional biases of the Garou Nation<br /> <br /> I'm contesting your assertions that it's really as hard as you're making it out to be after the knowledge of what the Ashtray did started to spread. You don't need to be some ultra badass, and it's only easier as the Skin Dancers grow and can start helping each other/prospective new members.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also the rite is a little harder than you think it is - you need to gather each hide under the same moon phase. </div> </div> </div>That's actually easier than I remember, not harder. Being able to take the hides of any Garou as long as it's the right moon is much easier than having to get Auspices involved too.<br /> <br /> Also... you can kill multiple Garou at a time for the rite. Nothing stipulates you need to do five different hunts (even if it is presented as the default way of doing it in the description of them in W20); though given some of the differing presentations of it I can at least accept that the Skin Dancers might not know it's easier than they think it is because so few have done it to have thought about refining the process.. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like I said before, pulling this off with even a vaguely competent Sept... </div> </div> </div>Again, the setting (at least pre-W5) was moving in this direction as the Skin Dancers started to spread. There are a lot of level 1-2 Septs around, where there are going to be gaps in what Gifts and Rites they have compared to the big major Septs. It's not a matter of superior intellect or tactics... just patience for when shit hits the fan (like a major Wyrm attack) to pin the death of your target on in a fashion that's unlikely to be questioned (or at least questioned soon enough). Smaller Septs might not even have the powers necessary to figure it out without traditional investigation skills, and they still need a reason to use them, as the ones that just activate on their own are exceedingly rare.<br /> <br /> If you can find Ronin to hunt down, even better, because no, the Garou are not keeping close enough track of any local Ronin to notice or care if a few got themselves killed by something else out there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Plus if you are able to pick the easiest targets and hunt them down efficiently with minimal risk that only furthers the point I'm making; you met your objective with the smartest strategy available and you've shown skill in backing up your idea, hunting down the best possible candidates for an easy execution. Again, skills the Garou Nation could have benefited from. </div> </div> </div>The only point that this supports, is that the Skin Dancers being more than a one off antagonist makes sense in the setting... which nobody was contesting.<br /> <br /> I seriously do not get what you're driving at here. The core topic was if the Skin Dancers become a Tribe in full, could a Skin Dancer renounce the Tribe, and if so could they potentially be cleansed of the taint from their creation and join a a traditional Tribe. Nobody was going around saying, &quot;man, what's wrong with these people, the very idea that they'd exist in the setting is non-sense.&quot; We got off on a tangent of how can they even achieve Tribe status/be a Tribe (again, whether they did it or not depends which books you're on). <br /> <br /> Nobody is saying anything that needs constant reminding that the Garou are assholes to the kinfolk as a culture, and in extreme cases this has lead to such negativity that some kin are willing to become Skin Dancers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-23T02:47:20-07:00","id":1495473,"title":"","content":"My headcanon: In times long gone the rite of sacred rebirth was a reasonably common Gaian ritual used by the garou to reward kinfolk and bolster the strength of their families. The skins used would be of those punished, those killed in war, or those who volunteer them after death depending on the time and place. During these times the wolves did not have a great many external threats and so they often turned inwards: with the garou being greedy, self-serving and arrogant a lot of corruption occurred and many needless deaths were caused because some people in power wanted to ensure their own offspring could get enough pelts. The problem became so pervasive that the garou decided the ritual and it's practitioners needed to be expunged.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think there's a potentially practical use for the rite in modern times. People donate when they die, maybe if the garou can look past their pride (extremely unlikely) they can donate skin. If the taint could be dealt with the BSDs also have a lot of cannon fodder and are likely to get slaughtered in groups of five or more so you could maybe get 2-6 new garou after clearing out a hive.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ultimately, renown is too important for most Garou. I imagine some tribes like the Get, GW, Uktena or Shadow lords being more open to it. But they're likely to remain secretive about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 10-23-2022, 05:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-31T07:54:28-07:00","id":1495972,"title":"","content":"I do want to make something known about the kinfolk that seek to become Skin-Dancers. The only thing they need to do is cast the ritual, so have 5 dots in Rituals so they can be taught the ritual. They, <i>themselves</i> don't need to actually go out and kill the werewolves anyone can do that. Infact they don't even need to be recent as per the text:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Ritual of Sacred Rebirth</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This rite allows the caster to become a Garou, but only after successfully <b>gathering the skins of five Garou</b> ... <b>The pelts may be years apart, so long as they are always preserved in the proper way</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine. The Caster doesn't need to kill the Garou themselves it doesn't call for it just needs the pelts, and the pelts don't even need to be fresh. This is further put to the point in the W20 Skinner module with these lines:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>W20 Skinner SAS</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Skin Dancers were careful to lie low after Haight\u2019s death. They knew the Garou Nation would be swift to hold them accountable for his crimes \u2014 to say nothing of their own. <b>They still recruited new members by collecting skins when they could, but they were always careful to dispose of the bodies afterwards.</b><br /> <br /> The Vulture Walkers want to increase their ranks. Most don\u2019t mind the idea of getting some payback from the Garou at the same time. <b>They plan to achieve this by gathering more skins,</b> preferably under a common moon, and by recruiting more disaffected Kinfolk who might be able to learn the Rite of Sacred Rebirth.<br /> <br /> In the basement, the pack will find <b>the skins the Vulture Walkers have been gathering.</b> They may find all the skins claimed from Black Spiral Dancer corpses as well as those taken from the recent murders, or <b>some may be missing if the Vulture Walkers had a fresh recruit in their ranks.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine. This seals the fact that the kinfolk doesn't need to be involved in the killings. Just needs the ability to learn the Ritual itself. So, these kinfolk are not badass geniuses that have the ability to kill full Garou but, instead Kinfolk that are hunted by the Skin-Dancers and them brought into the fold with pelts taken from BSD and other Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12895,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","user":"MrNatas","date":".  But of spelling and grammar corrections 10-31-2022, 10:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-31T13:26:15-07:00","id":1496004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494970-rite-of-renunciation-and-skin-dancers?p=1495972#post1495972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This seals the fact that the kinfolk doesn't need to be involved in the killings. Just needs the ability to learn the Ritual itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my chronicles, I even allow such stitched together pelts to be passed down from one kinfolk to the next. These &quot;magic pelts&quot; are often kept as heirlooms passed down from one generation to the next within certain families of lost kinfolk. (In my chronicles, Samuel Haight is simply someone who rediscovered the lost secret of how to do so, but there were Skindancers going back to the Stone Age after the Impergium, and the secrets of how to become one get learned and forgotten in many cycles now). These families or secret societies are one reason for the old lore of people becoming werewolves by putting on magic wolfskins.<br /> <br /> That is definitely a house rule for a faction that is for NPC antagonists, but I feel that falls into line for the concept.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}